//? Title: ConvNeXt V2: Global Response Normalization and Visible Atto Fitting
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Modern convolutional blocks combine large depthwise spatial filters with expanded channel
processing. We check the normalization or layer-scale rule, distinguish analytic model budgets
from executed forwards, then expose every tensor Adam update of a complete Atto classifier.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.5_attention_and_modern_convnets/convnext_v2.cpp`.

> The method

V2's response normalization uses G_c=sqrt(sum_H,W X_c²), N_c=G_c/(mean_channels G+1e-6),
then Y=X+gamma*X*N+beta. Gamma and beta start at zero, making the layer exactly identity.
Its safe square-root argument defines the norm derivative at zero as zero, avoiding 0*infinity
NaNs for dead channels. At active affine values, gradients include normalized-response effects.
Multiplying X by a positive scalar only APPROXIMATELY preserves N because epsilon stays fixed.
The pictured fixture checks all-zero/single-dead-channel initialization and active affine values.
V2's fully convolutional masked-autoencoder pretraining is not implemented by this classifier.

Both versions use biased depthwise 7×7 filtering, channels-last LayerNorm (epsilon 1e-6),
a pointwise expansion to 4C, exact erf GELU, pointwise projection and raw shortcut addition.
V1 scales the projected branch by a learned channel vector initialized to 1e-6; V2 instead
inserts GRN between expanded GELU and projection. Filters and classifier use untruncated
N(0,.02), biases zero, an initialization adaptation from the released truncated normal.
There is no BN or moving-statistics store. Per-example inverted branch dropout increases
linearly from zero to drop_path at the LAST block, using i/(n−1), and is absent in inference.

A biased 4×4/4 patchify convolution with LayerNorm starts the reference network. Three
LayerNorm plus biased 2×2/2 joins connect four stages. Global mean, LayerNorm and a classifier
finish it. The report prints analytical learned counts for every released table entry, checking
those formulas against actual full-weight Atto/Tiny 64-pixel forwards and a Tiny 224-pixel
forward. The other large designs are not allocated; Huge's count does not require allocating
its roughly 2.6 GB Float32 weights. Exact reference MACs use 56/28/14/7 stage sides and exclude
normalization/nonlinearity/GRN/addition/memory work. They are not latency measurements.

The full-width Tiny backward probe retains all eighteen blocks at 64 pixels. It activates V1
layer scales or V2 GRN affine entries to inspect learned-branch derivatives, separately from the
near-identity initialization fixture. All parameter-tensor derivatives must be finite and above
a relative diagnostic threshold; this fixture does not guarantee nonzero gradients for arbitrary
inputs. All model computations, preprocessing, losses and updates use the tensor library.

The visible fit retains the complete Atto layout, depths 2/2/6/2 and widths 40/80/160/320,
with a 2×2/2 CIFAR patchify stem, ten classes and drop_path=.1. It uses 128 fit/64 validation/
64 official-test images, 8 batch-eight epochs, explicit Adam(.001) and kernel L2=.0001/2,
with padded crops/flips. Validation selects learned parameters; no moving state exists to save.
The two versions have 3376290/3389170 learned scalars in this setting. These bounded runs do
not reproduce the paper's AdamW, longer schedules, stronger augmentation or pretraining.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/convnext_v2_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/convnext_v2_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/convnext_v2_concept.tikz > build/convnext_v2_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/convnext_v2_concept.svg build/convnext_v2_concept.dvi > build/convnext_v2_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
